WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.880
Does Christian hope mean you should be

2
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:05.800
finished crying?

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.580
Romans eight says believers who have

4
00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.480
the Spirit still groan.

5
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.160
We’re waiting for the redemption

6
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.020
of our bodies.

7
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.680
Our hope reaches toward resurrection.

8
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.560
God intends to redeem this wounded,

9
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:19.560
mortal life.

10
00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.060
That future gives us reason to wait,

11
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.080
even while loss still hurts.

12
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.620
So when Romans twelve calls us

13
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.080
to weep with those who weep,

14
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.580
sharing tears doesn’t mean we’ve forgotten

15
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:31.120
our hope.

16
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.340
When you sit beside someone grieving,

17
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.440
you can speak gently of what God

18
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.760
has promised and still let them mourn.

19
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:38.900
In Christ,

20
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.020
we wait for a future we don’t

21
00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:41.540
yet see.

22
00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.580
Hope can make room for tears,

23
00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.680
and love can stay beside them.
